# ---- interpretation / caveats
I=r['interpretation']; a=I.find('Q3: At the common 10" beam'); b=I.find(' | Q12 (round 2)')
new=('Q3 (round 4): the 10" HCN and HCO+ 2-1/3-2/4-3 ladders at the centre are fitted by sub-thermal, warm gas: Tk > ~56 K (84%; >~28 K at 95%; no upper bound, the median depends on the Tk ceiling of the prior), n < ~1e5 (97.5%; lower end set by the prior), HCN column 2-3x HCO+ at equal filling (degenerate with the HCN/HCO+ filling ratio), thick HCN (tau_HCN32 > 1 at 78%), eta ~ 0.02. These are one-zone beam averages with a 10%/band flux scale shared by all positions; the earlier tight joint result (Tk=152 K, n 4.62 [3.62,4.88]) overstated the constraint (independent calibration per position). N vs S vs Bridge is NOT testable at 10": the apertures overlap (N-S 5.1", weight 0.48), 56-72% of the 3-2 flux is shared smooth gas, and an intrinsic core contrast of 2 is diluted to 8-14% (a 2-sigma detection would need >=4), so identical 10" ladders are guaranteed and say nothing about the nuclei; they remain consistent with the 1" N/S differences. At 6.5" T43/T32 N/S is 1.10-1.16 (indicative). The only 10" contrast with power is E1 vs centre: HCN T21/T32 1.46x and T43/T32 0.48x (3.9-6.5 sigma with common calibration; HCO+ 1.18x, 0.76x at 3-5 sigma), P(Tk_E1<Tk_centre)=0.94 (HCN alone 0.91, HCO+ alone 0.64), E1 Tk<~56 K; E2 and W are unconstrained. J=1-0 intensities at 1.7" (Harada+2018, assumption-labelled) disfavour thin HCN at S (0.26->0.04) and leave N undecided; the compact components are thick with A_N/A_S~3, consistent with team-a p0009 (HCN column or excitation difference at S; n and Tk differences not required). Abundance is not measured: N(H2) is known to +-1 dex per X(HCO+), which itself spans 1 dex. A cold (10-35 K), thick or dense-thin branch is not excluded by the ladder (chi2 differences <=4) and needs a physical argument (Tk >= Tdust, CO Tb).')
if a>=0 and b>a: I=I[:a]+new+I[b:]
elif 'Q3 (round 4)' not in I: I+=' | '+new
r['interpretation']=I
cav=[c for c in r['caveats'] if not c.startswith('Q3r4:')]
cav.append('Q3r4: single-zone RADEX with one eta per position; the 10" ladders are beam averages of compact cores plus a shared smooth component (cores hold 14-38% of the HCN 3-2 flux), so n, Tk, A are not nuclear values; the grid is converged at 0.1 dex in N and A (0.2 dex changes the lower Tk edge); N-S-Bridge posteriors are identical by construction; the joint centre fit uses a product-of-marginals truncation of the per-position eta; J=1-0 intensities are literature values at 1.7" with different uv coverage; Brunetti+2021 pressures, cloud sigma and CO brightness temperatures are quoted from the review and were not re-checked; E2 and W are prior-dominated.')
r['caveats']=cav; r['results']=res
json.dump(r,open(R,'w'),indent=1); print(len(res))
